WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.160
Contract Reviews holds the synthetic agreement and its later amendment.

2
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:20.100
Typed by Claude (automated test) as contract manager: submits through MCP.

3
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:42.980
The amended cap appears in the comparison with the fictional playbook.

4
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:56.540
The report quotes the replacing clause and its parsed cap value.

5
00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:22.840
AI locates clause identifiers; code checks keywords, amendments, values and playbook positions.

6
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:33.760
The review workflow waits for a decision on its report version.

7
00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:42.920
DataIQ, iMBrace's records workspace, holds the report-version decision records.

8
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.360
Typed by Claude (automated test) as lawyer: opens the decision form.

9
00:01:48.800 --> 00:02:01.800
Typed by Claude (automated test) as lawyer: records rejection and fallback request.

10
00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:07.400
Saving the decision starts the board automation for this report.

11
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:25.840
Find the decision record for this synthetic review.

12
00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:33.440
The matching decision resumes the waiting contract-review workflow.

13
00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:56.000
The review returns the fallback request from the automated lawyer-role decision.

14
00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:17.080
DataIQ keeps the fictional playbook thresholds used by the comparison.
